&lt;h2 id=&#34;in-case-on-openshift-less-than-42&#34;&gt;In case on OpenShift less than 4.2&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenShift uses an arbitrarily assigned user ID when it starts a container.
Starting from OpenShift 4.2, it also inserts that user into &lt;code&gt;/etc/passwd&lt;/code&gt; for using by the application inside the container,
but before that version, the assigned user is missing in that file. That blocks workloads of &lt;code&gt;ghcr.io/pipe-cd/piped&lt;/code&gt; image.
Therefore if you are running on OpenShift with a version before 4.2, please use &lt;code&gt;ghcr.io/pipe-cd/piped-okd&lt;/code&gt; image with the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
